<title>NORWAY: RGI wins 120 mln crown shipbuilding deal.</title>
<headline>RGI wins 120 mln crown shipbuilding deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian shipyard Brattvaag Skipsverft, a subsidiary of investment group RGI ASA, has won a 120 million Norwegian crown contract to build a platform supply vessel for Gulf Offshore, Oslo Bourse said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The ship is to be delivered in March 1998.</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
